---
// US-SITE-12: what this site does with visits (nothing but the host's access logs), and what hlabs itself sends.
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy" description="This site has no analytics, no cookies and nothing from other sites. Here's what is kept.">
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="backdrop" aria-hidden="true"><div class="gridbg"></div></div>
    <div class="wrap prose" style="position: relative">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="h1">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 16px">For everyone who visits hlabs.h4loom.com.</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It sets no cookies and has no analytics, trackers or ads.</li>
        <li>
          It loads nothing from other sites: its fonts and pictures come from here. Links to other sites, like GitHub,
          take you there only when you follow them.
        </li>
        <li>
          Search in the help runs in your browser. What you type isn't sent anywhere.
        </li>
        <li>
          The light or dark theme you pick is kept in your browser, not sent to us.
        </li>
        <li>
          The site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, it keeps standard access logs (your IP address, the
          page, the time and your browser) for up to 30 days, to keep the site running and safe. We don't use them for
          anything else.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>hlabs itself</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>There's no account with us: the admin account you make lives on your own computer.</li>
        <li>
          hlabs sends no usage data. It goes online to check for updates, to refresh the App Store's list and download
          the apps you install, and for the services you turn on yourself, such as remote access or cloud backups.
          Settings › Advanced › What hlabs connects to lists each one.
        </li>
        <li>
          Downloads come from GitHub Releases and the apps' own image registries, which keep their own logs.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Ask on <a href="https://github.com/haribrothers/hlabs/issues">GitHub</a>. hlabs is open source, so you can also
        read exactly what it does.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div style="height: 64px"></div>
</Page>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 760px;
  }
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 44px 0 12px;
  }
  .prose li,
  .prose p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--site-muted);
  }
  .prose ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
